# Cloud credentials for the desktop renderer.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) to build a desktop app that can sign in.
# Without them the build is local-first and complete: documents, search, Quick
# Note and the dock all work, and the account screen says there is no account
# service rather than pretending otherwise.
#
# Vite inlines these at build time, so they travel inside the packaged
# application. That is what makes them workable here at all — `process.env`
# belongs to the machine that ran the build, and a packaged app launched from a
# Start menu inherits none of it.
#
# Both are public by design. The anon/publishable key is safe in a shipped
# bundle because Row Level Security, not secrecy, is what protects the data.
# The `service_role` key is not public and must never appear here.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-key

# There is deliberately no VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY.
#
# Sign-up is not possible from the desktop: Turnstile issues a token against
# the hostname that served the widget, and a packaged renderer is served from
# `file://`, which has no hostname. The app sends people to the web application
# to create an account and signs them in here afterwards, which needs no bot
# check. `WEB_APP_URL` in the environment overlay is where it sends them.
